Subject: Container health check: postgres --healthcheck (and --pg_isready) in the one-file server
Purpose: The image has no shell and no pg_isready, so a Docker HEALTHCHECK or the healthcheck of a Compose file had nothing to run. "postgres --healthcheck" is pg_isready, linked into the executable as embedded_pg_isready_main, with the defaults of the image (POSTGRES_USER and POSTGRES_DB, the _FILE forms too; PGHOST and PGPORT through libpq) and a status Docker understands: 0 when the server accepts connections, 1 otherwise (Docker reserves 2). "postgres --pg_isready [options]" is plain pg_isready for other checks, as "--psql" is psql. The temporary server of the first start listens only on a socket inside the data directory, so it does not count as healthy. An image built without pg_isready reports that, as it does for the other tools. This is a patch of its own on top of 0900 and for 17 and later, as the dump tools of the "full" image are; the releases before 17 have no health check.
Components: src/backend/main/embedded.c
Checks: image/native-production-test.sh P18 (status 0 on a running server, 1 with no response or a wrong port, plain pg_isready through --pg_isready, and a Docker Compose service with the exec-form healthcheck that becomes healthy under "up --wait")
Origin: own
Targets: native
Releases: 17.0-

--- a/src/backend/main/embedded.c
+++ b/src/backend/main/embedded.c
@@ -68,6 +68,7 @@
